.TH IMUD.CONF 5 "2026-07-31" "imud 1.8" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
imud.conf \- configuration file for the imud IMU daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
.br
.I ~/.config/imud/imud.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud.conf
is a TOML-like text file that controls all aspects of
.BR imud (8):
which sensors to use, MEKF filter parameters, output stream destinations,
magnetic declination, and logging.
.PP
.B imud
searches for the configuration file in this order:
.PP
.RS 4
1. Path given on the command line with
.B \-\-config
.br
2.
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
.br
3.
.I ~/.config/imud/imud.conf
.RE
.SS Syntax
.TP
Sections
.B [section_name]
on its own line.
.TP
Key\-value pairs
.IB key \ = \ value
.TP
Comments
.B #
to end of line; inline comments are allowed.
.TP
Strings
Must be double-quoted:
.BR "driver = \(dqism330dhcx\(dq" .
Paths beginning with
.B ~/
are expanded to
.IR $HOME/ .
.TP
Integers
Decimal or hexadecimal
.RB ( 0x6B ).
.TP
Booleans
.B true
or
.BR false .
.TP
Arrays
Comma-separated values in brackets; used only for
.BR rotation_euler_deg .
.SS Reload semantics
Keys marked
.B [restart]
below take effect only after a full daemon restart.
.br
Keys marked
.B [hot]
are applied live by sending
.B SIGHUP
to the daemon
.RB ( "sudo systemctl reload imud" ).
.SH SECTIONS
.SS [device]
Hardware bus selection.
.B [restart]
.TP
.B i2c_bus
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq/dev/i2c-1\(dq)
I2C bus device node.
.TP
.B gpio_chip
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqgpiochip0\(dq)
gpiochip device name.
Use
.B gpiochip0
on Raspberry Pi 4 and
.B gpiochip4
on Raspberry Pi 5 (RP1 GPIO controller).
.TP
.B sim_file
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq)
An .imucap capture for the sim driver to replay (with
.B driver
= \(dqsim\(dq in both
.B [imu]
and
.BR [mag] );
empty selects the built-in synthetic scenario.
.B imud --replay
.I FILE
is the shortcut form.
See
.BR imud (8)
and docs/capture.md.
.TP
.B sim_loop
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Repeat the capture forever; sequence numbers and timestamps are rebased so
downstream consumers see a continuous stream.
.TP
.B sim_speed
.RI (float,\ default:\ 1.0)
Playback pacing: 2.0 is double speed, 0 delivers as fast as the pipeline
accepts (offline regression runs).
.SS [imu]
IMU driver settings.
.B [restart]
.TP
.B driver
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqism330dhcx\(dq)
Driver name:
.BR ism330dhcx ,
.BR icm20948 ,
.BR icm42688p ,
.BR lsm6dso ,
.BR lsm6dsox ,
.BR mpu9250 ,
.BR mpu9255 ,
or
.B sim
(software simulation, no hardware required).
Drivers other than
.B ism330dhcx
and
.B sim
are experimental (register map verified from datasheet; not yet validated
on hardware).
.TP
.B i2c_addr
.RI (int,\ default:\ 0x6B)
I2C address.
ISM330DHCX: 0x6B (SA0 high) or 0x6A (SA0 low).
.TP
.B int_gpio
.RI (int,\ default:\ 17)
BCM GPIO number for the FIFO watermark interrupt.
Set
.B 0
to use a 10\~ms polling timer instead.
.TP
.B odr_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 833)
Output data rate in Hz.
The driver rounds to the nearest supported rate.
ISM330DHCX supports: 12, 26, 52, 104, 208, 416, 833, 1660.
.TP
.B accel_g
.RI (int,\ default:\ 8)
Accelerometer full-scale range in g.
ISM330DHCX: 2, 4, 8, 16.
.TP
.B gyro_dps
.RI (int,\ default:\ 2000)
Gyroscope full-scale range in degrees/second.
ISM330DHCX: 125, 250, 500, 1000, 2000, 4000.
.TP
.B fifo_wm
.RI (int,\ default:\ 64)
FIFO watermark in sample-sets.
At 833\~Hz, 32 ~= 38\~ms latency; 64 ~= 77\~ms.
.SS [mag]
Magnetometer driver settings.
.B [restart]
.TP
.B driver
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqmmc5983ma\(dq)
Driver name:
.BR mmc5983ma ,
.BR ak09916 ,
.BR ak8963 ,
.BR lis3mdl ,
.BR lis2mdl ,
or
.BR sim .
Drivers other than
.B mmc5983ma
and
.B sim
are experimental.
.TP
.B i2c_addr
.RI (int,\ default:\ 0x30)
I2C address.
MMC5983MA has a fixed address (0x30).
The AKM compasses inside a 9-axis IMU
.RB ( ak09916
in the ICM-20948,
.B ak8963
in the MPU-9250/9255) are reached through the host chip's I2C
.IR bypass ,
not its I2C master, and answer on the host bus at 0x0C.
.TP
.B int_gpio
.RI (int,\ default:\ 27)
BCM GPIO for the measurement-done interrupt.
Set
.B 0
to use a polling timer.
.TP
.B odr_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 100)
Output data rate in Hz.
MMC5983MA supports: 1, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 1000.
.TP
.B set_period_s
.RI (float,\ default:\ 5.0)
Interval in seconds between degauss (SET/RESET) pulses.
Set
.B 0
to disable.
.SS [fusion]
MEKF noise parameters and rejection thresholds.
.B [hot]
.PP
The mekf_* values are tuned constants, not raw sensor readouts:
mekf_gyro_noise and mekf_gyro_bias build the filter's process noise Q,
held deliberately above the measured sensor floor.
The per-unit noise recorded by
.B imud-cal characterize
(cal.json \(dqnoise\(dq section) is informational only and never feeds
the filter.
.TP
.B mekf_gyro_noise
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.007)
Gyro noise density in rad/s/sqrt(Hz).
.TP
.B mekf_gyro_bias
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.00015)
In-run gyro bias instability in rad/s.
.TP
.B mekf_accel_noise
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.0022)
Accelerometer noise density in m/s^2/sqrt(Hz).
This describes SENSOR noise only. Resist the temptation to raise it to
"account for wave acceleration" \(em that is what
.B mekf_wave_accel
below is for.
Across the 12-seed wave benchmark the default is a sharp local optimum for
the marine (yaw-only) configuration, and values in the range 0.003 to 0.03
are substantially worse than either side of it: the gravity correction
weakens, the filter leans on gyro integration, gyro-bias observability
degrades, and the growing errors feed back through the innovation gate.
The
.B nis_accel
field on the wire reports whether the noise model matches reality (1.0 =
consistent); check it against a real capture before changing this.
Must be greater than zero \(em zero or negative is rejected at load, since it
would make the Kalman gain degenerate.
.TP
.B mekf_mag_noise
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.0004)
Magnetometer noise density in Gauss/sqrt(Hz).
.TP
.B mekf_wave_accel
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.8)
Steady-state standard deviation, in m/s^2, of the wave-orbital acceleration
that contaminates the gravity measurement in a seaway. This is the knob for
"the sea is rough", not
.BR mekf_accel_noise .
.IP
The disturbance is correlated over roughly a second rather than white, so it
is modelled as a first-order Gauss\(enMarkov process in the filter state.
Without that, the filter treats 833 strongly correlated samples per second as
833 independent measurements of gravity, collapses its own covariance and
diverges. Set to 0 (or set
.B mekf_wave_accel_tau_s
to 0) to disable the state entirely, which returns the pre\-1.7 six\-state
filter exactly.
.IP
Too small a value is the failure mode that hurts, so round up. Run
.B imud\-cal fit\-ra
on a capture of your worst conditions: it measures the disturbance with the
state disabled and prints a suggested value.
.TP
.B mekf_wave_accel_tau_s
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.5)
Correlation time, in seconds, of the Gauss\(enMarkov wave-acceleration state.
0 disables the state.
.IP
Not to be confused with
.BR wave_tau_s ,
which is the unrelated sea\-state reporting window.
.IP
Attitude error and wave acceleration are separated only by their dynamics, so
too long a value lets the state absorb genuine tilt: the benchmark's yaw\-only
attitude RMS degrades from 2.3 degrees at 0.5 s to 7.1 degrees at 2 s. Short
is the safe side.
.TP
.B mekf_mag_dip_sigma_deg
.RI (double,\ default:\ 1.0)
Uncertainty, in degrees, of the magnetic reference's DIP angle.
.IP
Applies only to 3\-D vector fusion
.RB ( mag_yaw_only
= false), where the field's dip is what constrains roll and pitch. The dip of
the reference is fixed once, at alignment, from the tilt estimate available at
that moment; in a seaway that is wrong by around a degree, and in this mode the
error becomes a permanent roll/pitch bias.
.IP
It cannot be corrected in run. The reference's in\-run healing is gated on the
platform being quiescent, deliberately: the accelerometer samples that pass the
motion gate in a seaway are wave\-phase correlated, and learning from that
subset walks the reference away from the truth rather than toward it (measured
over 30 minutes; opening the gate roughly triples the covariance
inconsistency). So the error is admitted into the covariance instead, as a
rank\-1 term along the one direction a dip error acts on.
.IP
The default is the residual measured after a 5 s
.BR align_window_sec ,
rounded up. Set to
.B 0
when a position source supplies WMM field invariants \(em that removes the dip
error at its source and is strictly better. Raising it improves covariance
consistency and lowers the
.B nis_mag
wire field, by design: the dip channel is being trusted less.
.TP
.B mag_reject_gauss
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.05)
Strong-anomaly cutoff: reject magnetometer updates whose post-calibration
residual exceeds this value (Gauss). Fine-grained consistency is handled by
internal chi-squared innovation gates; keep this a coarse threshold
(~10% of the Earth field).
.TP
.B accel_skip_thresh
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.05)
Skip accelerometer updates when
.RI |a|\(en1g
exceeds this fraction of g.
.TP
.B mag_yaw_only
.RI (bool,\ default:\ true)
Heading-only magnetometer fusion (marine default): the magnetometer corrects
heading and never pulls on roll/pitch. Set
.B false
for full 3D vector fusion (magnetically clean installs with a true 3D
calibration).
.TP
.B heave_tau_s
.RI (float,\ default:\ 12.0)
Heave filter time constant, seconds. Vertical displacement from band-passed
double integration of vertical acceleration; feeds the $PASHR heave field
and the binary packet heave_m. Allow ~2 minutes settling after startup.
.B 0
disables.
.TP
.B wave_tau_s
.RI (float,\ default:\ 120.0)
Sea-state averaging window, seconds: significant wave height, mean
zero-crossing wave period, and the vessel's roll and pitch periods and
significant single amplitudes are exponentially weighted statistics of the
heave/roll/pitch oscillations over this window. Statistics settle ~2 windows
after the heave estimator itself settles. Requires
.B heave_tau_s
> 0.
.B 0
disables (the packet fields read 0.0).
.TP
.B engine_vibration_g2
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.0)
EMA threshold (m^2/s^4) for engine-vibration detection.
Set
.B 0
to disable.
.TP
.B engine_accel_skip_thresh
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.20)
Accelerometer skip threshold override applied while engine vibration is
detected (wider gate; accel noise is additionally inflated 4x).
.SS [capture]
Black-box recording of every raw sensor sample to rotating .imucap
files \(em replayable with
.B imud --replay
and analyzable with
.BR imud-cal (8)
.BR characterize / fit-temp .
All keys
.BR [restart] .
See docs/capture.md for the format and sizing (\(ti25 MB/hour at 104 Hz).
.TP
.B enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Record raw samples from both sensors, exactly as the drivers delivered them
(pre-mount, pre-calibration).
.TP
.B dir
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq/var/lib/imud\(dq)
Destination directory; files are named imud-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.imucap (UTC).
.TP
.B max_mb
.RI (int,\ default:\ 256)
Start a new file when the current one reaches this size.  0 = unlimited.
.TP
.B max_files
.RI (int,\ default:\ 8)
Keep at most this many capture files, deleting the oldest.  0 = keep all.
.TP
.B flush_s
.RI (int,\ default:\ 5)
Interval between flushes to storage.
.SS [calibration]
.B [restart]
.TP
.B file
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq/etc/imud/cal.json\(dq)
Path to the calibration file produced by
.BR imud-cal (8).
Supports
.B ~/
expansion.
.TP
.B startup_settle_sec
.RI (double,\ default:\ 5.0)
Seconds to discard sensor output after chip initialisation.
Set
.B 0
for the
.B sim
driver.
.TP
.B gyro_bias_sec
.RI (double,\ default:\ 2.0)
Length of the stationary bias-estimation window at startup.
Set
.B 0
to skip.
.TP
.B align_window_sec
.RI (double,\ default:\ 5.0)
Seconds of accelerometer and magnetometer averaging used for the one\-shot
initial attitude alignment.
.IP
Whatever tilt error survives this window is baked permanently into the magnetic
reference's dip, so in a seaway the length matters. One second \(em the value
hardcoded before 1.7 \(em is about a fifth of a typical roll period, so it
aligns to an arbitrary point in the cycle: measured attitude RMS in the marine
default is 47.7 degrees at a 1 s window against 2.19 degrees at 5 s, flat
beyond. 3\-D vector fusion keeps improving out to roughly 15 s.
.IP
The only cost of a longer window is startup latency before the filter produces
usable attitude, so raising it is worthwhile when starting from a mooring and
not when starting underway.
.SS [nmea]
NMEA 0183 output over UDP and/or a TCP listener.
Both are off by default (since 1.6 a stock daemon emits only on the local
.B [stream]
socket; every network output is an explicit opt-in).
.B [restart]:
.BR enabled ,
.BR dest_addr ,
.BR dest_port ,
.BR tcp_enabled ,
.BR tcp_bind_addr ,
.BR tcp_port .
.B [hot]:
.BR rate_hz .
.TP
.B enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Enable NMEA UDP output.
.TP
.B rate_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 10)
Output rate in Hz (shared by UDP and TCP).
.TP
.B dest_addr
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq255.255.255.255\(dq)
Destination IP address (broadcast, unicast, or multicast).
.TP
.B dest_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 10110)
Destination UDP port.
.TP
.B tcp_enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Enable the NMEA-over-TCP listener.
Chartplotter apps (OpenCPN, Navionics, phone/tablet nav apps) connect as TCP
clients and each receives every sentence burst; up to 8 clients, slow clients
skip bursts rather than stalling the daemon.
.TP
.B tcp_bind_addr
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq0.0.0.0\(dq)
Listener bind address (numeric IPv4).
Set
.B 127.0.0.1
to keep the listener host-local.
.TP
.B tcp_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 10110)
Listener TCP port (the de-facto NMEA-over-TCP port).
.PP
Sentences emitted:
.BR $PASHR ,
.BR $HCHDM ,
.BR $HCHDG ,
.BR $TIROT ,
.BR $IIXDR .
When declination is configured,
.B $HCHDT
(true heading) is added and
.B $HCHDG
carries the variation fields.
.SS [highrate]
High-rate binary UDP stream.
.B [restart]:
.BR enabled ,
.BR dest_addr ,
.BR dest_port ,
.BR coord_frame .
.B [hot]:
.BR rate_hz .
.TP
.B enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Enable the high-rate stream.
.TP
.B rate_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 500)
Output rate in Hz.
.TP
.B dest_addr
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq239.255.0.1\(dq)
Destination IP.
Default is an IPv4 multicast group (TTL=1, link-local).
Use
.B 255.255.255.255
for broadcast or a unicast IP for point-to-point.
.TP
.B dest_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 10111)
Destination UDP port.
.TP
.B coord_frame
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqNED\(dq)
Output frame:
.B NED
(North-East-Down) or
.B ENU
(East-North-Up).
.SS [stream]
Local AF_UNIX subscription stream carrying the same 276-byte binary packets
as
.B [highrate]
over a SOCK_STREAM socket: loss-free for same-host consumers, up to 8
subscribers. Slow consumers get dropped packets (visible as imu_seq gaps),
never a stalled daemon.
An optional TCP listener serves the same framed packets to remote consumers.
.B [restart]:
.BR enabled ,
.BR socket ,
.BR tcp_enabled ,
.BR tcp_bind_addr ,
.BR tcp_port .
.B [hot]:
.BR rate_hz .
.TP
.B enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ true)
Enable the subscription stream \(em the one output a stock daemon provides
(the bridges and libimud consumers read it).
.TP
.B socket
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq/run/imud/imud-stream.sock\(dq)
Listen socket path (mode 0660).
.TP
.B rate_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 100)
Per-subscriber packet rate in Hz (shared by AF_UNIX and TCP subscribers).
.TP
.B tcp_enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Enable the TCP listener: the same framed packets, lossless, over the
network \(em for a remote
.BR imud-mon ,
a bridge on another machine, or any
.BR libimud (3)
consumer using
.B imud_connect_tcp
(Python:
.BR ImudClient.connect_tcp ).
.TP
.B tcp_bind_addr
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq0.0.0.0\(dq)
Listener bind address (numeric IPv4).
Set
.B 127.0.0.1
to keep the listener host-local.
.TP
.B tcp_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 10112)
Listener TCP port.
.SS Bridge daemons
The optional bridge daemons \(em
.BR imud-signalk (8),
.BR imud-mqtt (8),
.BR imud-influxdb (8),
.BR imud-mavlink (8),
.BR imud-prometheus (8)
\(em are each configured by their own file,
.IR /etc/imud/imud-<name>.conf ,
documented in
.BR imud-signalk.conf (5),
.BR imud-mqtt.conf (5),
.BR imud-influxdb.conf (5),
.BR imud-mavlink.conf (5),
and
.BR imud-prometheus.conf (5).
They are not part of
.IR imud.conf .
(The
.B signalk_*
keys under
.B [position]
are unrelated \(em imud reading position
.I from
Signal K.)
.SS [mount]
Board-to-body rotation.
.B [restart]
.TP
.B rotation_euler_deg
.RI (array,\ default:\ [0.0,\ 0.0,\ 0.0])
Rotation as [roll, pitch, yaw] in degrees.
Applied as R = Rz(yaw) x Ry(pitch) x Rx(roll).
Only the yaw component is normally non-zero; set it to correct for
the angle between the chip X axis and the vessel bow.
Exactly three values are required; a shorter or longer array is a
fatal configuration error.
.TP
.B rotation_matrix
.RI (array\ of\ 9,\ unset)
Board-to-body rotation given directly, row-major, as
v_body = R x v_board.
An alternative to
.B rotation_euler_deg
for installations whose rotation is known as a matrix.
Validated at load against R^T R = I and det(R) = +1;
a non-orthonormal matrix or a reflection (det = -1, typically a
sign-flipped axis) is a fatal configuration error.
.TP
.B preset
.RI (string,\ unset)
Named rotation shortcut.
One of:
.BR identity ,
.BR yaw_90 ,
.BR yaw_180 ,
.BR yaw_270 ,
.BR roll_90 ,
.BR roll_270 ,
.BR pitch_90 ,
.BR pitch_270 .
Overrides
.B rotation_euler_deg
when set; whichever mount key appears last in the file wins.
An unrecognised preset name is a fatal configuration error \(em
starting with a silently wrong mount rotation would bias every sample.
.SS [logging]
.B [hot]:
.BR level ,
.BR stats_hz .
.B [restart]:
.B file
(path changes; the file itself is reopened on every reload).
.TP
.B level
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqwarn\(dq)
Log verbosity:
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warn ,
or
.BR error .
.B warn
is recommended for production (SD card friendly).
.B info
adds lifecycle messages and a periodic
.B [stats]
heartbeat.
Applied live on SIGHUP.
.TP
.B file
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq)
Log destination.
Empty = write to stderr; under systemd, lines carry sd-daemon priority
prefixes so journald records real priorities.
Set an absolute path to redirect to a timestamped log file; the file is
reopened on SIGHUP, so logrotate can rotate it
.RB ( "postrotate: systemctl reload imud" ).
Repeated identical messages are suppressed and logged as a count.
.TP
.B stats_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 1)
Rate of the
.B [stats]
heartbeat line.
Only visible at
.B info
or
.B debug
level.
.SS [position]
Magnetic declination and true heading.
.B [hot]:
declination_deg, lat_deg, lon_deg, wmm_file (declination and the WMM field
reference are recomputed on SIGHUP; a live position source \(em gpsd or
SignalK \(em owns declination while enabled).
.B [restart]:
the gpsd_* and signalk_* source keys and fix_max_age_h.
.PP
When declination is active, imud emits
.B $HCHDT
in NMEA and sets
.B FLAG_DECLINATION_VALID
(with the
.B declination_deg
field) in the binary packet.
.PP
Three modes (highest priority wins):
.TP
1.\ WMM\ auto-compute
Set
.B lat_deg
and
.B lon_deg
(both non-zero).
imud loads
.B wmm_file
and computes declination at startup and on SIGHUP.
Accurate to \(+-0.5\(de for a fixed installation.
.TP
2.\ Static\ override
Set
.B declination_deg
only (leave lat/lon at 0.0).
East declination is positive (+), west is negative (\-).
.TP
3.\ Disabled\ (default)
All three values at zero.
.PP
Configuration keys:
.TP
.B declination_deg
.RI (float,\ default:\ 0.0)
Static magnetic declination in degrees.
Ignored when
.B lat_deg
and
.B lon_deg
are both non-zero.
.TP
.B lat_deg
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.0)
Geodetic latitude in decimal degrees (+N / \-S).
Set with
.B lon_deg
to enable WMM auto-compute.
.TP
.B lon_deg
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.0)
Geodetic longitude in decimal degrees (+E / \-W).
.TP
.B wmm_file
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq\ =\ auto)
Path to the WMM coefficient file.
When empty (the default), imud uses
.I /etc/imud/WMM.COF
if it exists (operator override), otherwise
.I /usr/share/imud/WMM.COF
(installed by the imud-wmm-data package /
.BR "make install-wmm-data" ).
The bundled model is WMM2025, valid 2025.0\(en2030.0.
When WMM2030 is published (expected late 2029), update the data package \(em
or drop the new file in as an override:
.EX
    sudo cp WMM2030.COF /etc/imud/WMM.COF
    sudo systemctl reload imud
.EE
.TP
.B gpsd_enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Connect to gpsd for live position updates.
.TP
.B gpsd_host
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqlocalhost\(dq)
Hostname or IP address of the gpsd instance.
.TP
.B gpsd_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 2947)
TCP port of the gpsd instance.
.TP
.B signalk_enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Poll the SignalK REST API for position (every 30\~s).
.TP
.B signalk_host
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqlocalhost\(dq)
Hostname or IP address of the SignalK server.
.TP
.B signalk_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 3000)
HTTP port of the SignalK server.
.TP
.B signalk_path
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq/signalk/v1/api/vessels/self/navigation/position\(dq)
REST endpoint path.
.TP
.B fix_max_age_h
.RI (float,\ default:\ 24.0)
Hours to retain a GPS-derived declination without a new fix.
An anchored vessel with continuous GPS reception keeps its declination
indefinitely; the TTL only fires during a genuine GPS outage.
Set
.B 0
to never expire.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
System-wide configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/imud/imud.conf
Per-user override.
.TP
.I /etc/imud/cal.json
Calibration data written by
